 ## Background
-The term "transfer function" was adopted from signal processing but defined in volume visualization as an operation mapping scalar values to color, opacity, and material values [S6, unofficial]. Levoy's work on ray casting established the foundational pipeline where classification/transfer functions map raw voxel values to material properties [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It is widely used in medical imaging (CT, MRI) and scientific visualization to reveal internal structures [S6, unofficial][S9, unofficial][S13, unofficial]. Libraries like VTK provide specific classes (`vtkPiecewiseFunction`, `vtkColorTransferFunction`) to implement these functions [S13, unofficial][S14, unofficial].
